IQ-TREE3-GPU — a GPU likelihood backend for IQ-TREE 3
=====================================================

This project is a patch/derivative of IQ-TREE 3 and therefore inherits IQ-TREE's license:

    GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE, Version 2 (GPL-2.0)

The full GPL-2.0 text is distributed with IQ-TREE and is available at
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt — it applies in its entirety to this work.

What is covered
---------------
- src/iqtree3_gpu.patch and src/gpu_new_files/ (gpu_kernels.cu, gpu_kernels.h, phylotreegpu.cpp)
  are modifications and additions to IQ-TREE 3 source; the resulting combined binary is GPL-2.0.
- The benchmark/figure/verification scripts and documentation in this repository are released under
  the same GPL-2.0 terms for consistency with the tool they support.

Attribution / how to cite
--------------------------
If you use this tool, please cite both:
  - IQ-TREE 3: Wong T.K.F., Ly-Trong N., Ren H., Demotte P., Baños H., Roger A.J., Susko E., Bielow C.,
    De Maio N., Goldman N., Hahn M.W., dos Reis M., Vinh L.S., Huttley G., Lanfear R., Minh B.Q. (2026)
    IQ-TREE 3: phylogenomic inference software using complex evolutionary models.
    Mol. Biol. Evol. 43(5):msag117, https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msag117
    (source: https://github.com/iqtree/iqtree3)
  - This work: Cho B., Kostic A.D. (2026) IQ-TREE3-GPU: GPU-accelerated maximum-likelihood phylogenetic
    tree inference for complex amino acid substitution models. Version 0.1.0.
    https://github.com/kosticlab/iqtree3-gpu (mirror: https://github.com/terry-b-cho/iqtree3-gpu).
    Citation metadata are in assets/CITATION.cff. When quoting a performance number, also
    cite the exact GPU card used, as reported in the figures/tables.

No warranty
-----------
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, as stated in the GPL-2.0. The one
correctness guarantee we make and verify is scientific equivalence to CPU IQ-TREE (identical
log-likelihood, topology RF=0, and support); run scripts/iqtree3-gpu-verify.sh to confirm it on your
hardware before relying on a result.
